🔹 APPROACH 2 (OPTIMAL) - CORE ALGORITHM:
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

enqueue(x):
    input.push(x)

dequeue():
    if output.isEmpty():
        while !input.isEmpty():
            output.push(input.pop())
    return output.pop()

front():
    if output.isEmpty():
        while !input.isEmpty():
            output.push(input.pop())
    return output.peek()

empty():
    return input.isEmpty() && output.isEmpty()

🔹 WHY LAZY TRANSFER WORKS:
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Input Stack: [1, 2, 3] (3 on top) - newest elements
Output Stack: [] (empty)

Transfer when output is empty:
    Pop 3, 2, 1 from input
    Push 3, 2, 1 to output
    Result: Output [3, 2, 1] (1 on top)

Now output has oldest elements on top → FIFO! ✅
Don't transfer again until output is empty!

🔹 COMPLEXITY SUMMARY:
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Operation  │ Approach 1  │ Approach 2 ⭐ │ Explanation
───────────┼─────────────┼───────────────┼─────────────────────
enqueue    │ O(n)        │ O(1)          │ Just push to input
dequeue    │ O(1)        │ Amortized O(1)│ Lazy transfer
front      │ O(1)        │ Amortized O(1)│ Same as dequeue
empty      │ O(1)        │ O(1)          │ Check both stacks
Space      │ O(n)        │ O(n)          │ Two stacks

🔹 KEY INSIGHT:
───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Each element goes through exactly 3 operations:
1. Push to input stack (during enqueue)
2. Move to output stack (during first dequeue after enqueue)
3. Pop from output stack (during dequeue)

Total: O(3) = O(1) per element amortized! 🎯

